(7764498, 1286969, 123833, '<td valign="top">
<table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Neat:</b></div><hr/><i> The quality of the photo is not the best,  you have some clear cloning issues along the top edge of the limo - but I''m sure loving your message! Climate change, the biggest hoax of the century! </i></td></tr></table> You missed Big Oil Lies, Anita.</td>', 'Originally posted by Neat: The quality of the photo is not the best,  you have some clear cloning issues along the top edge of the limo - but I''m sure loving your message! Climate change, the biggest hoax of the century!  You missed Big Oil Lies, Anita.', '2024-03-04 00:45:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(7764499, 1286947, 138630, '<td valign="top">
<table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Neat:</b></div><hr/><i> Not sure why the whole photo is not in colour, not a big fan of select desaturation. The blown out part underneath the car is distracting also. My eyes keep veering there. I do like the motion on the wheel however. </i></td></tr></table>
<br/>
<br/>The photo isn''t in color because I converted it to black and white; it was a black car and the road was basically black - the only hint of color was a bit of gold on the wheel rim - not sure what you mean by selective desaturation here.  <a href="https://www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1287151" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img border="0" src="https://images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/135000-139999/138630/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1287151.jpg" xalt="'' . substr(''https://images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/135000-139999/138630/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1287151.jpg'', strrpos(''https://images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/135000-139999/138630/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1287151.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''"/></a>   Unless you thought the "Firestone" lettering was on the car in the first place?  I worked hard to find a font that I thought came as close as possible to that of the company''s logo - I''d be pleased to think I was successful at that :) 
<br/>
<br/>I added the red Firestone to identify the product I was "advertising" and and the red border because I thought it gave the photo a more finished look for a billboard.  I agree that the bright area under the car is distracting - the light was not good and this certainly isn''t a great photo, but I wanted to play so I put it in :)
<br/>
<br/>ETA: And now I see that the best place for the red FIRESTONE lettering would, in fact, have been right under the car - on the bright area that draws the eye!
<br/><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2024-03-04 10:06:00.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by Neat: Not sure why the whole photo is not in colour, not a big fan of select desaturation. The blown out part underneath the car is distracting also. My eyes keep veering there. I do like the motion on the wheel however. 

The photo isn''t in color because I converted it to black and white; it was a black car and the road was basically black - the only hint of color was a bit of gold on the wheel rim - not sure what you mean by selective desaturation here.     Unless you thought the "Firestone" lettering was on the car in the first place?  I worked hard to find a font that I thought came as close as possible to that of the company''s logo - I''d be pleased to think I was successful at that :) 

I added the red Firestone to identify the product I was "advertising" and and the red border because I thought it gave the photo a more finished look for a billboard.  I agree that the bright area under the car is distracting - the light was not good and this certainly isn''t a great photo, but I wanted to play so I put it in :)

ETA: And now I see that the best place for the red FIRESTONE lettering would, in fact, have been right under the car - on the bright area that draws the eye!', '2024-03-04 01:00:31.000000', '2024-03-04 10:06:00.000000', 0),
